==Analysis==
While there were few Republicans who voted for Turek in 2026, Turek won independents by 20%. However, 10% of Trump voters in 2024 backed Turek, while very few Harris voters backed Hinson.<ref>{{cite news |title=How Democrats flipped the Senate blue: The ABC News Voter Poll tells the story |url=https://abcnews.com/Politics/democrats-flipped-senate-blue-abc-news-voter-poll/story?id=137840395 |access-date=November 10, 2026 |publisher=ABC News |date=November 4, 2026}}</ref> Additionally, [[Rob Sand]]'s landslide victory in the [[2026 Iowa gubernatorial election]] may have produced [[coattail effect]]s that helped Turek.<ref>{{cite news |title=Turek's Iowa win exposes the trap Trump set for Republicans {{!}} Opinion |url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/opinion/columnist/2026/11/03/iowa-election-results-turek-flips-senate-democrats/92582985007/ |access-date=November 10, 2026 |publisher=USA Today |date=November 4, 2026}}</ref>

